Package: headsetcontrol
Architecture: amd64
Depends: ${shlibs:Depends}, ${misc:Depends}, udev
Description: Control USB headsets: battery, sidetone, lights and more
 HeadsetControl reads and sets what a USB gaming headset's own firmware
 offers and its manufacturer's program does not give to Linux: the battery
 level, sidetone, lights, the inactive time, the equaliser presets and the
 chat-mix dial, for the headsets of Logitech, SteelSeries, Corsair, HyperX,
 Razer, Audeze, Astro and others (headsetcontrol --help lists what a connected
 headset supports).
 .
 The package installs the program and the udev rules that give the person
 at the desktop the headset's device files (headsetcontrol -u writes them from
 its own device list). It is built from the release's source, not from
 upstream's prebuilt program.
 .
 Sparky Stereo OS, Daniel Ramos's edition of SparkyLinux (by Pawel "pavroo"
 Pijanowski). Upstream: Denis Arnst (Sapd) and the HeadsetControl contributors.

Package: headsetcontrol-dev
Section: libdevel
Architecture: amd64
Depends: ${misc:Depends}, libhidapi-dev
Description: HeadsetControl as a library: headers and static library
 The C++ and C interfaces of HeadsetControl (headsetcontrol.hpp,
 headsetcontrol_c.h) and the static library the program is linked from, for
 programs that want to read a headset's battery or set its sidetone
 themselves.
